2026-09-23 — TODO K03 bounded diagnosis, not full-test acceptance.

The installed, unchanged memslot_modification_stress_test is invoked through
the existing selftest-init/boot workflow. The fixed Neoverse-N2 EL2 contract,
four host vCPUs, 4 GiB RAM, Images and test executable are identical between
these controls. Each guest test uses one vCPU and mode 3 (PA48/VA48/4K).
No compiler or kernel repair is installed by this diagnostic.

Untraced reduction: -m 3 -b 64M -i 2; original TAP 1/1 and shutdown PASS
on both kernels. This is not the default 1 GiB/all-mode/10-iteration test,
which remains subject TIMEOUT at the unchanged 120-second limit.

For the 256 KiB reduction (-m 3 -b 256K -i 2), the fixture runs the original
ELF and traces kvm_arch_flush_shadow_memslot and kvm_free_stage2_pgd. It bounds
each trace file at 2 MiB and rejects empty traces, overruns and dropped events.
Both depth controls have four page-table destructions and two invalidations,
zero losses on all four CPUs, original exit 0, inner TAP PASS and shutdown PASS.

                              GCC               EvoCC
depth 6 whole test, ns         259443008          1718397008
depth 1 whole test, ns         208469008          1274434992
depth 6 destruction sum, us    16845.008          292145.000
depth 1 destruction sum, us    3898.000           81147.990
depth 6 invalidation sum, us   880.992            1624.992
depth 1 invalidation sum, us   250.000            605.984

These are individual instrumented observations, not statistical benchmarks.
Depth-one traces avoid tracing nested helpers (including EvoCC's non-inlined
helpers); they still expose excess time in page-table destruction, not just
memslot invalidation. This does not explain the entire elapsed-time difference:
destruction accounts for only ~81 ms of the subject's ~1.27 s. Scheduling and
tracing remain confounders. Inclusive nested durations must not be added.
Next: isolate the repeated page-table helpers as ordinary C code, preserve
their memory/guard behavior, and test any code-generation repair independently.
K03 remains OPEN until the original full workload on repaired Images passes.

Build: sealed linux/arm64, network none, GCC 14.2.0-19,
  gcc-14 -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -DKVM_PROFILE_MEMSLOT=1
    '-DKVM_PROFILE_DEPTH="1"' tests/fixtures/kvm-demand-fault-profile.c
Depth 6 uses the default KVM_PROFILE_DEPTH. Both diagnostic mode branches
compile with warnings as errors. The original ELF is extracted byte-for-byte
from the retained reference runtime; its hash matches the selftest build.
The ftrace control writer handles short writes because frozen ftrace_graph_write
consumes one whitespace-delimited filter per write; no filter is silently lost.

Boot environment, both sides:
  K1_ALLOW_QEMU_DRIFT=1
  K1_KERNEL_CONTRACT=contracts/kernel-selftest-kvm-target.json
  K1_BOOT_LANE=tcg-neoverse-n2-el2 K1_KUNIT_AUTORUN=0 K1_BOOT_TIMEOUT=90
  K1_INITRAMFS=.build/k7-coverage/repair-runtime/kvm-memslot-profile/payload.cpio
  K1_TEST_DISK=.build/k7-coverage/repair-runtime/scratch.img
  tools/k1/boot.sh IMAGE RUN_DIRECTORY
Existing parse_transcript validates the inner test using each boot's nonce.
The 64 MiB scratch disk is opened snapshot=on; no large runtime copy is made.

